 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DeuYgZJIgUm/",
 "title": "Four S-Tier Habits for Serious Salespeople",
 "topic": "sales",
 "summary": "Riad Mourssali outlines four core habits designed to help salespeople close more deals and maintain control of their schedule. The advice focuses on proactive morning prospecting, instant lead response, critical call analysis, and targeted learning applied directly to calls.",
 "key_points": [
  "Dedicate the first hour of every day to a non-negotiable call block reserved strictly for new conversations, avoiding messages or other people's problems.",
  "Call incoming leads immediately with zero delay between seeing the lead's name and dialing.",
  "Enable loud alert notifications exclusively for new leads while muting all other notifications during your call block.",
  "Review call recordings that challenge you rather than stroke your ego, specifically analyzing moments where you struggled or froze on objections like 'let me think about it.'",
  "Read just one book per month targeting the specific issue currently costing you deals, rather than endlessly collecting tips you never implement.",
  "Write down the exact phrasing from your reading and test it on your next 10 calls."
 ],
 "content": "Post caption:\nTry these S-Tier habits!\n\nTranscript:\n\"S-tier habits for people who take sales seriously. Number one is a non-negotiable call block. First hour of your day is new conversations only. No messages, no reacting to other people's problems they hand you, you set the pace. Number two is calling new leads the second they come in. There should be no gap between seeing the name and hitting the call. It sounds hard, but just turn on loud alerts for new leads, and mute every other notification during your call block. Number three is call review that actually challenges you, not reassures you. There is a difference between rewatching your best close and sitting through the call where you froze on let me think about it. And lastly, one book per month. And I'm not saying one book minimum. Most salespeople save so many tips, they never use any of them. Pick the one thing costing you deals right now, read on that, write down the exact words you'll try, and say them on your next 10 calls. Start using these, and if you want to learn from an S tier closer, follow me for more.\"\n\nOn-screen text:\n- S-Tier Habits (for people who take sales seriously)\n- Book shown: Atomic Habits by James Clear\n- iPhone focus mode settings screen showing 'Work On' and 'Do Not Disturb'\n- Audio recorder app screen showing 'New recording 3' and 'New recording 2'\n- Instagram profile: @riad.mourssali (\"12+ years in sales taught me more than how to sell\")",
 "status": "done",
